# PUBLIC DATA. This file contains an OpenPGP *fingerprint* — an identifier,
# not key material. It is the same string published at
# https://launchpad.net/~bceverly/+editpgpkeys and served by
# keyserver.ubuntu.com to anyone who asks. Nothing here is secret, and nothing
# here can sign anything.
#
# The private half lives in a password vault and in the
# LAUNCHPAD_GPG_PRIVATE_KEY GitHub secret, and nowhere else. It is never
# written into this repository in any form.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Which key signs tmd's source packages for the Launchpad PPA.
#
# Pinned here, in the repository, rather than taken from DEBSIGN_KEYID in the
# environment. That variable is global to a shell, and a developer who
# maintains more than one package has one value in their profile for whichever
# project they set up first: tmd's first clean-chroot build was signed by a key
# called "Milsurp Monitor Package Signing" for exactly that reason. Which key
# signs this project is a property of this project.
#
# To use a different key for one build without editing this file:
#     TMD_SIGNING_KEY=<fingerprint> make deb-source
#
# Format: one full 40-character fingerprint. Comments and blank lines ignored.

